You are a senior product designer and frontend engineer. Build GRANTLY, a unified scholarship discovery and management platform, as a complete, deployable, award-level web app for a 6-hour individual frontend hackathon. Judges score: (1) UI/UX and visual quality, (2) functionality, (3) creativity, (4) alignment with the problem, (5) code quality, (6) responsiveness and accessibility. Optimize for all six.

==================================================
0. THE PROBLEM (verbatim from the organizers)
==================================================
"Accessing educational financial assistance can be a complicated journey for students. Finding relevant opportunities, understanding available options, navigating application processes, and keeping track of important information can often create unnecessary challenges. Design and build a modern digital solution that addresses the challenges associated with discovering and managing educational financial assistance. The objective is to transform a complex experience into a seamless digital journey."

The brief names four pains. Build the whole product around four pillars and name them in the UI:
  1. DISCOVER: find relevant scholarships fast.
  2. UNDERSTAND: see plainly whether I qualify and why.
  3. APPLY: know exactly what to prepare and in what order.
  4. TRACK: one place for deadlines, documents, notes and status.
"Unified" means one profile, one search, one tracker, one calendar across many providers (government, university, foundation, corporate, NGO).

==================================================
1. HARD RULES (non-negotiable)
==================================================
- Modern framework required. Use React 18+ with Vite and TypeScript (strict mode). No vanilla-only code.
- Styling: Tailwind CSS with all design tokens defined as CSS custom properties. Animation: Framer Motion (the "motion" package). Icons: lucide-react. Dates: date-fns. Routing: react-router-dom. State: Zustand with the persist middleware (versioned, with a migrate function). Drag and drop: @dnd-kit (with a full keyboard and button alternative).
- No backend. Use mock data and localStorage. Keep a thin async data layer (src/lib/api.ts) so a real backend could replace it later.
- Must be original. Do not imitate any existing scholarship site, brand, logo or copy. All providers and scholarships are fictional.
- `npm install && npm run build` must succeed with zero TypeScript errors and zero console errors or warnings in the browser. Pin dependency versions. Do not use packages you are unsure exist.
- Be responsive from 320px to 2560px wide.
- Use no external images and no external runtime assets except fonts. Every visual is CSS, SVG or generated. If any asset fails to load, the layout must still hold.
- Never output lorem ipsum, TODO placeholders in the UI, dead links, or buttons that do nothing. If a feature is out of scope, remove the control.

==================================================
2. BUILD ORDER (so a cutoff never leaves a broken app)
==================================================
Work in phases. After each phase the app must run.
 P0 (must ship): project setup, design tokens, layout shell, routing, data + types, Discover, Scholarship detail, profile with match scoring, Tracker, 404, SEO files, accessibility basics.
 P1: Dashboard, Calendar/deadlines, Compare, Contact form + Thank-you, Privacy, Terms, Cookie banner, analytics, loading and error states everywhere, dark mode.
 P2 (polish): command palette (Cmd/Ctrl+K), print styles, export/import data, micro-interactions, empty-state illustrations.
If output length is limited, finish P0 completely, then say exactly which phase you stopped at so I can ask you to continue.

==================================================
3. DESIGN DIRECTION: "quiet confidence, editorial warmth"
==================================================
Feel: a beautifully typeset university prospectus crossed with a calm, trustworthy fintech tool. Elegant, spacious, human. Never a generic SaaS template. A stressed student should feel relief on first sight.

TYPOGRAPHY
- Display: "Young Serif" (headlines, big numbers, scholarship titles on detail pages).
- Body/UI: "Schibsted Grotesk" (variable).
- Data/deadlines/amounts: "JetBrains Mono" with tabular numerals.
- Load through @fontsource packages (preferred) so fonts are bundled, or Google Fonts with preconnect and font-display: swap. Define robust fallback stacks (Georgia / system-ui / ui-monospace) with size-adjusted fallbacks to prevent layout shift.
- Do NOT use Inter, Roboto, Arial, or Space Grotesk as the primary face.
- Fluid type scale with clamp(). Ratio about 1.25. Body 16 to 17px, line-height 1.6, measure 60 to 72ch. Headlines tight (line-height 1.05 to 1.15, slight negative tracking). Use text-wrap: balance on headings and text-wrap: pretty on paragraphs.

COLOR (define in OKLCH as tokens, light and dark)
- Never use pure #000 or #fff. Tint every neutral toward the brand hue.
- Light: background warm ivory about oklch(97.5% 0.012 85); surface slightly lighter; ink deep green-black about oklch(22% 0.03 165); muted text about oklch(48% 0.03 165); hairline borders at low contrast.
- Brand: deep pine green about oklch(42% 0.09 165) for primary actions and key emphasis.
- Accent: warm saffron about oklch(78% 0.15 78), used sparingly for deadlines, highlights and the match ring. One accent, used with restraint (about 10% of the surface).
- Semantic: success (green), warning (amber), danger (muted brick red), info (calm blue), each with accessible foreground/background pairs.
- Dark mode: deep green-black background (about oklch(18% 0.02 165)), never neutral grey, with re-tuned lower-chroma accents. Include a no-flash inline script in index.html that applies the saved or system theme before first paint. Provide a visible theme toggle (light / dark / system).
- All text must meet WCAG AA (4.5:1; 3:1 for large text and UI components) in both themes. Verify the saffron accent never carries small text on ivory.

LAYOUT AND SPACE
- 4px base spacing scale; use a rhythm of generous gaps between sections and tight gaps within groups. Vary spacing; do not use the same padding everywhere.
- Editorial composition: asymmetric hero, hairline rules, numbered sections ("01 Discover, 02 Understand, 03 Apply, 04 Track"), large serif numerals, plenty of whitespace.
- Max content width about 1200px, with a narrower reading column for text. Consistent 16px (mobile) / 24px / 32px+ gutters.
- Radii: one soft radius token (about 14px) plus a pill radius; stay consistent.

THINGS TO AVOID (common AI-design tells)
- No gradient text. No purple-to-blue gradients. No glassmorphism or heavy blur as decoration.
- No cards inside cards. No colored left-border stripes on cards or alerts. No grid of identical icon + heading + text cards as the main way to present features. No "hero metric" strip of three big numbers with tiny labels as filler.
- No modals unless unavoidable. Prefer inline expansion, drawers, popovers and dedicated pages.
- No emoji as icons. No em dashes in UI copy. No "Oops!", no exclamation-mark enthusiasm, no jargon.
- No bounce or elastic easing. No shadows stacked into muddy blobs: use one subtle, tinted, layered shadow token.

SIGNATURE DETAILS (give it a memorable identity)
- A "match ring": a slim circular SVG progress ring (saffron on pale track) showing match percentage, with the number set in the serif face.
- Deterministic generative thumbnail for each scholarship: an SVG pattern (arcs, grids, contour lines) seeded from the scholarship id and tinted with the brand palette. No two look the same, no external images.
- Deadline "time left" chips in mono type with urgency states: closed, closing within 7 days, within 30 days, later, rolling.
- A subtle paper grain on the background (inline SVG noise at very low opacity), turned off for prefers-reduced-transparency or print.
- Logo: a simple wordmark "Grantly" in the serif face with a small custom SVG mark (an abstract open book/compass point). Original, no existing logos.

MOTION
- Purposeful and quiet. Page-load staggered reveals (opacity + translateY 8 to 12px), 150 to 300ms, ease-out-quart cubic-bezier(0.25, 1, 0.5, 1). Animate only transform and opacity. Animate the match ring fill on first view. Smooth, short route transitions.
- Honor prefers-reduced-motion everywhere (disable transforms and parallax, keep instant state changes).
- Hover/press states on every interactive element: slight lift or tone shift, pressed state, 120ms.

