5. DATA MODEL AND MOCK DATA
==================================================
Types (src/types):
 Scholarship { id, slug, title, provider { name, type: 'government'|'university'|'foundation'|'corporate'|'ngo' }, summary, description, amount { min, max, currency, kind: 'one-time'|'annual'|'full-tuition' }, awards (count), deadline: { kind: 'fixed'|'rolling', offsetDays? }, levels[], fields[], eligibleCountries[] (or 'any'), residency?, minGpa?, financialNeed: 'required'|'considered'|'none', renewable, essayRequired, documentsRequired[], applicationSteps[], eligibilityCriteria[] (each machine-checkable AND human-readable), tags[], applyUrl (use a safe placeholder like '#' handled gracefully with an inline note, never a dead external link), sourceUpdated }
 Profile { name?, country, residencyCountry?, level, field, gpa?, gpaScale?, financialNeed, graduationYear?, interests[], completeness }
 Application { id, scholarshipId, status: 'saved'|'preparing'|'submitted'|'awarded'|'declined', checklist[{id,label,done}], notes, createdAt, updatedAt, submittedAt? }
Create at least 48 realistic, varied, FICTIONAL scholarships (diverse levels: high school, undergraduate, postgraduate, PhD; diverse fields; diverse countries including international-student-friendly and country-restricted ones; amounts from small to full-tuition; mixed essay/no-essay; mixed need-based/merit-based). Include edge cases on purpose: very long titles, very short descriptions, missing optional fields, no-GPA scholarships, rolling deadlines, deadlines tomorrow, already-closed deadlines.
IMPORTANT: store deadlines as day offsets from "today" and compute actual dates at runtime, so the demo never goes stale whether judged today or next month. Use the user's local time zone, handle date boundaries correctly, and never show "NaN" or "Invalid Date".

