6. FEATURES (build each fully)
==================================================
6.1 LANDING
- Above the fold on a 375x667 phone AND a 1440x800 desktop: headline, one sentence of support copy, a primary CTA ("Find my scholarships") and a secondary text link ("See how it works"). Headline example: "Every scholarship you qualify for, in one calm place."
- Composed hero visual built from SVG/CSS (e.g., a stack of award letters or a deadline timeline) that is not a stock-style illustration.
- Sections: the four pillars as an editorial numbered sequence; a live preview of real results from the mock data (a short list, not a card grid); "How matching works" in three plain steps; an FAQ using accessible disclosure components; closing CTA.
- Sticky mobile CTA: a bottom bar with the primary action that appears after scrolling past the hero, never overlaps the cookie banner or the bottom nav (manage stacking and safe-area insets), and hides on pages where it doesn't belong.

6.2 PROFILE AND ONBOARDING (/profile)
- Multi-step, skippable, under 60 seconds: country of citizenship, study level, field, GPA (optional, with scale), financial need, interests. Progress indicator, back/next, summary.
- Persist on every change. Show profile completeness. Explain why each question is asked.
- Worst cases: user skips everything (matching must still work with a clear "Add details for better matches" prompt), GPA outside valid range, unusual GPA scales, corrupt saved profile.

6.3 DISCOVER
- Instant search over title, provider, tags and fields with debounce. Highlight matches. Handle empty query, special characters, very long queries.
- Filters: level, field, country eligibility, amount range, deadline window, provider type, essay required, need-based, renewable. Active-filter chips with one-tap removal and "Clear all". Filters live in the URL so the view is shareable and the back button works.
- Sort: best match, deadline soonest, amount high to low, recently added.
- Toggle grid and list view. Result count announced via aria-live.
- Each result: generative thumbnail, title, provider, amount, deadline chip, match ring, 2 to 3 key eligibility facts, Save (bookmark) and Compare actions. Saving is optimistic with an undo toast.
- States: skeleton loading (simulate 400 to 900ms latency), zero results (suggest which filter to relax, with a one-tap action), error with Retry (include a hidden dev toggle or query param ?simulateError=1 to demonstrate), and "profile incomplete" nudge.
- On mobile, filters open in a full-height bottom sheet with an Apply button and live result count.

6.4 SCHOLARSHIP DETAIL (UNDERSTAND + APPLY)
- Serif title, provider, amount, deadline with exact date and time remaining, match ring.
- "Do I qualify?" panel: each criterion rendered as Meets / Likely / Check / Does not meet with a short plain-language reason and an icon plus text label (never color alone). Overall verdict first. Hard disqualifiers explained kindly with alternative suggestions.
- "How to apply": ordered steps, documents needed (checkable), estimated effort (e.g., "about 4 hours"), tips.
- Primary action: "Add to tracker" (creates an Application with a checklist generated from documentsRequired and steps). Secondary: Save, Compare, Share (copy link with confirmation), Print.
- Similar scholarships. Sticky mobile action bar (Add to tracker) that respects safe areas.
- Invalid :id shows a helpful not-found state with search suggestions, not a blank page.

6.5 MATCH SCORING (src/lib/matching.ts, pure and unit-testable)
- Deterministic weighted score (0 to 100) from level, field, country, GPA, need. Hard disqualifiers (wrong country, level, or GPA below minimum) cap the score and are labeled. Return { score, verdict, reasons[] } with human-readable reasons. Handle missing profile fields gracefully (unknown = neutral, flagged "Add X to improve this"). Write a few unit tests (Vitest) if the setup allows.

6.6 TRACKER (TRACK)
- Board with columns Saved, Preparing, Submitted, Decision. Drag and drop with @dnd-kit PLUS a "Move to" menu on every card (keyboard and screen-reader friendly) with announcements via aria-live. On mobile, show columns as swipeable tabs or a segmented control, not a squeezed 4-column board.
- Card: title, deadline chip, checklist progress bar, notes indicator. Opening a card shows a side panel/page with checklist, notes (autosave), key dates, link back to the scholarship, and "Mark submitted" / "Remove" (with undo, no blocking confirm dialog).
- Empty board: a warm empty state that links to Discover.
- Worst cases: removing an application, duplicate adds (prevent and explain), deadline passed while still "Preparing" (flag it gently), 50+ cards (stay performant).

6.7 DASHBOARD
- Greeting, profile completeness, next three deadlines, applications by stage, "potential funding in your tracker" total, top new matches, one recommended next action. No filler widgets. Skeletons while loading; meaningful empty states for new users.

6.8 CALENDAR / DEADLINES
- A month view AND an agenda list view (agenda is the default on mobile). Urgency styling, tap a deadline to open the scholarship. "Add to calendar" exports an .ics file for a deadline (generate client-side, correct time zone, escaped text).
- Past deadlines are visually muted and labeled "Closed".

6.9 COMPARE
- Up to 3 scholarships side by side: amount, deadline, level, field, countries, essay, need, renewable, your match. Highlight differences. On mobile, horizontal-scroll table with a sticky first column and clear scroll affordance. Remove items inline.

6.10 PERSISTENCE AND DATA SAFETY
- Zustand persist with a version number and migrate function. Wrap storage access in try/catch: if localStorage is blocked, full, or corrupt, the app must still work in memory and show a small non-blocking notice. Validate the loaded data shape and fall back to defaults instead of crashing.
- Profile page: Export my data (JSON download), Import (validate before applying), Reset everything (with clear explanation and undo toast window).

==================================================
7. QUALITY STATES (apply everywhere, no exceptions)
==================================================
- Loading: skeletons that match final layout (no layout shift), route-level fallback, button spinners with the label kept.
- Empty: every list and board has a helpful empty state with a next action.
- Error: ErrorBoundary, inline error with Retry, offline banner using navigator.onLine events.
- Forms: inline validation on blur and on submit, error text linked with aria-describedby, aria-invalid, focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, errors never rely on color alone, prevent double submit, preserve input on failure, clear success feedback.
- Long content: titles and provider names wrap or truncate gracefully with accessible full text; no overflow at 320px; no horizontal page scroll at any size.
- Interaction: every interactive element has default, hover, focus-visible, active and disabled states. Visible focus ring (2px, offset, brand colored, 3:1 contrast); never remove outlines without a replacement.
- Toasts: polite aria-live, auto-dismiss with pause on hover/focus, undo where relevant, never stacked more than 3.

==================================================
8. ACCESSIBILITY AND RESPONSIVENESS (scored criterion, so be rigorous)
==================================================
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA. Semantic landmarks (header, nav, main, footer), one h1 per page, no skipped heading levels, <html lang="en">.
- Everything operable by keyboard in a logical order, including drag and drop alternatives, bottom sheets (focus trap + Esc + return focus), menus and the cookie banner.
- Touch targets at least 44x44px. Text resizable to 200% without loss. Respect prefers-reduced-motion, prefers-color-scheme, and forced-colors (basic fallback).
- Alt text on every image. Decorative SVGs get aria-hidden and alt="" equivalents; meaningful SVGs get titles. The generative thumbnails are decorative (hidden from assistive tech) because the title is adjacent.
- Breakpoints: 320, 375, 480, 640, 768, 1024, 1280, 1536, 1920+. Mobile first. Test mentally at 320x568, 375x667, 768x1024, 1280x800, 1920x1080 and 2560x1440. Use container queries where a component's layout depends on its own width. Use dvh and env(safe-area-inset-*) so iOS browser bars and notches never hide actions.
- Performance: lazy-load routes, no unnecessary heavy libraries, memoize expensive lists, avoid layout shift, aim for Lighthouse 90+ on all four categories.

