- ESLint + TypeScript strict. Meaningful names. Comments only where intent is not obvious. No dead code, no unused dependencies, no console.log left behind.
- README.md: what it is, the four pillars, features, tech choices and WHY, folder map, how matching works, accessibility notes, how to run, how to deploy, environment variables, limitations (sample data, local-only storage), and what I would build next.
